    "result_text": "The full suite's only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and it passes.\n\nThe change is complete. Summary of what I did to satisfy the `email-unique` rule (reject creating an owner whose lower-cased email already belongs to another owner, returning 409):\n\n1. **`ClinicService`** \u2014 added `isEmailInUse(String email)` to the service interface, documented to mirror the existing `isTelephoneInUse` invariant.\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 implemented it as a read-only transactional method that normalizes the candidate email via `OwnerMapper.normalizeEmail` (lower-casing) and checks it against every existing owner's normalized email. A null/absent candidate email returns `false` (no conflict), matching the telephone check's style.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a conflict check right after the existing telephone duplicate check: if the email is already in use, respond `409 CONFLICT`.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` passes, and the full `./mvnw test` build is green.",
