    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is coherent, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- `isEmailInUse` sits in the service layer right next to its sibling `isTelephoneInUse` and follows that method's exact shape (normalize \u2192 null-guard \u2192 stream over `findAll()` \u2192 `anyMatch`), so a maintainer reads it as one of a family of \"is X in use\" checks rather than something new.\n- Normalization correctly reuses the existing `ownerMapper.normalizeEmail` qualifier that is already the canonical email-normalizer elsewhere (mapping config and the V1 update path), so no duplicated lowercasing logic is introduced.\n- The controller guard is placed alongside the other `CONFLICT` pre-checks in `addOwner`, matching the established one-check-per-`if` style and returning 409 as specified.\n- The interface Javadoc matches the style/depth of the neighboring methods.\n\nNo duplication, no catch-all growth, logic is in the right unit.",
